[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63436,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Wolffian tumour is a tumour of presumed mesonephric (Wolffian) origin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63437,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9110/1 Wolffian tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63438,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F33.Y &amp; XH2WJ5 Benign neoplasm of other specified female genital organs &amp; Mesonephric tumour NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63439,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> Wolffian adnexal tumour; Wolffian adenoma; retiform Wolffian adenoma; female adnexal tumour of probable Wolffian origin; mesonephric tumour NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63440,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63441,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "<p>Most arise in the broad ligament, with a subset developing in the ovary (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/108\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Wolffian tumour of the ovary</em>).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T08:17:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63442,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>Patients range in age from 19 to 83&nbsp;years (mean: 45&nbsp;years) and may present with abdominopelvic pain or abnormal bleeding; however, many cases are incidental findings {10414506}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-01T16:55:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63443,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are rare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63444,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63445,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A Wolffian origin is favoured because these tumours arise along the path of the regressing Wolffian system. <em>STK11</em>, <em>APC</em>, and <em>MBD4</em> mutations, as well as <em>KMT2D</em> variants, have been reported {30134342; 31591497}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63446,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "<p>Tumours are often well circumscribed and solid or solid and cystic, ranging in size from 0.8 to 30&nbsp;cm (mean: 6&ndash;10&nbsp;cm) {4693596; 10414506}. Haemorrhage, necrosis, or focal calcification may be seen.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-01T16:56:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63447,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>The tumours are composed of an admixture of hollow to solid tubules, sieve-like cysts, and diffuse (sometimes spindled) growth {4693596; 31591497}. Hyalinized bands may be prominent (imparting a nodular appearance) or delicate and interspersed within the stroma. Cells are cuboidal to ovoid, with scant cytoplasm, small nuclei, and inconspicuous nucleoli. Eosinophilic luminal secretions may be present; cytological atypia and mitoses are usually minimal.</p>\r\n<h5><em>Immunohistochemistry</em></h5>\r\n<p>Most are positive for broad-spectrum keratins, CK7, vimentin, CD10, inhibin, and calretinin, with variable expression of hormone receptors and SF1 {10414506; 26352548; 30134342}. EMA, GATA3, and PAX8 are typically negative but may show focal weak staining {26135559; 26352548}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:44:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63448,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63449,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63450,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> typically broad ligament or ovarian origin; tubular, sieve-like, or solid growth.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63451,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63452,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 212,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Aggressive behaviour (metastasis at diagnosis and/or recurrences) has been reported in rare cases. Features potentially associated with malignancy include hypercellularity, pleomorphism, and increased mitoses, but morphologically bland tumours have also recurred {12144833}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:43:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]